            "notes": "round 7 powers again, depend on the round 5 path.  play around with what you feel works best.  more than likely you'll have enough cash for all 6 epics.\n\nRen path:  [First Responder](item_30a5c70f-e0b5-489a-96ae-900f34c3823d)  combo'd with  [Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b).  superflexor gives you more WP and also will constantly be proc'd so long as you're healing.\n\nCrep path:  [Renaissance](item_a460f234-6434-4d47-99f9-d4a0b15cd591) to proc valk more often or  [Battle Medic](item_ccd0edff-4d57-4ac2-83a7-bab6ff0ffb2f) to increase dmg capabilities.  pair with  [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b) and/or  [The Closer](item_173c6d0f-dbe6-440e-924f-0ce08189ddce).\n\nProBeam and Distortion paths:  if you grabbed one of these 2 powers I would say get the other one or a different power that fits more with what you want to do this round.  so if you got Distortion, grab ProBeam, Crep, Ren, or FR.  generally i avoid powers like  [The Whambulance](item_67e91029-d0fc-4c9d-9733-ec7e1cc064a9), but  [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4) could be a good addition with ProBeam.\n\nsome other good items to grab if you're struggling to live are  [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8) and  [Blessed Boosters](item_957fd380-b7b4-40d4-8333-bb8c535ca931).  both add good survivability which is absolutely necessary late game.",
